  "problem": "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{6}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{6})=9.4623{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{9}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince ${9}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={9}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{\u2218}+9.4623{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{189}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={9}^{\u2218}$ and $x={189}^{\u2218}.$",
